# Codex Adversarial Review

Target: branch diff against 70d974c2ea060b3b7f7e7aaf073b7a0e672db664
Verdict: needs-attention

No-ship: this introduces an accessibility regression in the new tabbed map UI and replaces the old static index with dead buttons that advertise interaction but execute nothing.

Findings:
- [high] Tabbed map controls are not bound to any tab panels, so assistive tech has no programmatic relationship between the selected tab and the content that changes (src/components/mapa/PlanoViewer.tsx:39-115)
  `PlanoViewer` renders `Tabs.Root`, `Tabs.List`, and `Tabs.Tab`, but no `Tabs.Panel` at all. The map image and fullscreen content are rendered as ordinary elements later in the component, outside any tab panel semantics. Inference: Base UI expects tabs to control mounted panels, and without them the selected tab has no associated `tabpanel` for screen readers or keyboard users. The visible floor changes, but that state change is not exposed through the tabs pattern, which is a user-facing accessibility regression on a public page.
  Recommendation: Render each floor's content inside `Tabs.Panel` elements keyed by the same values as the tabs, or otherwise provide an explicit accessible relationship (`aria-labelledby`/live region) so the selected tab is tied to the displayed map and index.
- [medium] Every index entry is now a focusable button with an explicitly empty click handler (src/components/mapa/IndiceItem.tsx:9-14)
  Each zone in the index is rendered as a `<button>` even though the handler body contains only a TODO comment and performs no action. That means keyboard and screen-reader users encounter a list of controls that announce as interactive but do nothing when activated. This is a regression from the previous static list markup and creates a misleading UI on the main navigation surface for the map.
  Recommendation: Do not ship these as buttons until they have real behavior. Revert them to non-interactive list content, or implement the promised selection/highlight behavior and expose the state change accessibly.

Next steps:
- Convert the floor switcher to a complete tabs pattern with `Tabs.Panel` content for each floor and verify screen-reader behavior.
- Remove or fully implement the zone-item button interaction before release.
